    {
      "id": "5797988e-2bde-4d71-88fd-1fff07ab7af7",
      "type": "architecture_note",
      "content": "Suggested implementation: check the argument string before conversion to usize, set a boolean (arg.starts_with(\"0\")) in the Args struct, pass it to the printer, and use an if condition to determine the format string.",
      "confidence_score": 0.6,
      "status": "unconfirmed",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "id": "9e0a1223-9eff-4ffe-9de2-706d4f67e06b",
          "source_type": "github_pr",
          "external_id": "723",
          "url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/723",
          "excerpt": "i think you would want to have it check the argument string before conversion to `usize` and set a boolean in the `Args` struct to `arg.starts_with(\"0\")`. Then you would pass that boolean to the printer and just have an `if` condition determine the format string to use",
          "fetched_at": "2026-07-27T17:58:14.190276Z",
          "workspace_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
        }
      ],
